This repository is a research and preliminary-design tool.

The current implementation primarily addresses two-dimensional reinforced-concrete frame models.

Important limitations include:

the principal structural workflow is intended for RC structures;
steel-section analysis is not currently fully integrated;
the retrofit optimization uses linear structural analysis for candidate screening;
the planar directional models do not represent the complete behaviour of a three-dimensional building;
torsional response and full 3D diaphragm effects require a three-dimensional model;
nonlinear member behaviour, cyclic degradation, and collapse mechanisms require more advanced nonlinear modelling;
shear-wall foundations and wall-to-existing-structure connections require separate engineering verification;
retrofit constructability must be checked by the engineer;
cost results are comparative estimates and are not contractor quotations.

The results should therefore support, rather than replace, engineering judgement.

Final retrofit design should be independently verified using the applicable standards, National Annexes, nonlinear analysis procedures where required, and project-specific material, detailing, geotechnical, architectural, and construction information.
